1
00:00:03,232 --> 00:00:10,154
[SPEAKER_00]: So, we can go through ānāpānasati sutta now, which is a Majjhima hundred and eighteen.

2
00:00:12,435 --> 00:00:13,575
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of breathing.

3
00:00:33,548 --> 00:00:58,822
[SPEAKER_00]: It says that, on one occasion, the Buddha was living at Savatthi, in the Eastern Park, in Migara's mother's place, with many well-known elder disciples, Venerable Sariputta, Maha Mughalana, Maha Kasuppa, Maha Kacchayana, Maha Kotika, Maha Kapina, Maha Chunda, Venerable Anuruddha, Venerable Ananda, together with other well-known elder disciples.

4
00:01:00,925 --> 00:01:09,749
[SPEAKER_00]: So, those disciples, those elders bhikkhus, were exhorting, instructing junior bhikkhus, eh... sometimes ten, twenty, thirty, forty bhikkhus at a time.

5
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:17,433
[SPEAKER_00]: And those junior bhikkhus, being exhorted, being instructed, sooner or later understood the Noble Attainments.

6
00:01:24,596 --> 00:01:26,857
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, the Buddha said that, eh...

7
00:01:29,151 --> 00:01:35,953
[SPEAKER_00]: Upon the completion of pavārana, on the full moon of the 15th poster day, the Buddha was sitting down in the open, surrounded by the bhikkhu saṅgha.

8
00:01:37,094 --> 00:01:43,936
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, the Buddha, having surveyed the completely silent saṅgha of bhikkhus, addressed the bhikkhus, I'm resolved upon this path of practice.

9
00:01:44,036 --> 00:01:46,937
[SPEAKER_00]: My mind is resolved upon this path of practice.

10
00:01:47,017 --> 00:01:55,120
[SPEAKER_00]: Therefore, bhikkhus, make even more of an effort to reach the unreached, to attain the unattained, to realize the unrealized.

11
00:02:03,349 --> 00:02:13,756
[SPEAKER_00]: And the bhikkhus from the countryside returned to Savatthi to see the Buddha, and then the other bhikkhus continued to exhort junior bhikkhus 10, 20, 30, 40 at a time.

12
00:02:15,277 --> 00:02:27,965
[SPEAKER_00]: So, eh... on the next full moon, eh... on the full moon night of Komudi, the fourth month, the Buddha was sitting down in the open, surrounded by bhikkhu saṅgha.

13
00:02:28,366 --> 00:02:31,828
[SPEAKER_00]: Having completely surveyed the silent saṅgha bhikkhus, he addressed the bhikkhus.

14
00:02:34,106 --> 00:02:36,768
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, bhikkhus, disassembly is free from chit-chat.

15
00:02:37,009 --> 00:02:39,591
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, disassembly is free from the idle chatter.

16
00:02:39,831 --> 00:02:41,773
[SPEAKER_00]: Purity has been established in its essence.

17
00:02:42,794 --> 00:02:44,355
[SPEAKER_00]: Such is this saṅgha of bhikkhus.

18
00:02:45,516 --> 00:03:00,849
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that, eh... that clearly indicates that the saṅgha of the bhikkhus that the Buddha was praising was, eh... basically an ārya saṅgha, which means there were no putujanas there.

19
00:03:01,049 --> 00:03:01,590
[SPEAKER_00]: There were no...

20
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:12,943
[SPEAKER_00]: In this saṅgha of bhikkhus, there are arahants, with thanes destroyed.

21
00:03:13,903 --> 00:03:22,649
[SPEAKER_00]: Having come to an end, done what should be done, laid down the burden, reached the cause of peace, with the fetters of existence wasted away, liberated by right understanding.

22
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:26,551
[SPEAKER_00]: Such is this saṅgha of bhikkhus.

23
00:03:26,591 --> 00:03:30,934
[SPEAKER_00]: In this saṅgha of bhikkhus, there are bhikkhus with five lower fetters wasted away,

24
00:03:33,322 --> 00:03:38,185
[SPEAKER_00]: Such is this saṅgha of bhikkhus.

25
00:03:38,225 --> 00:03:50,472
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, in this saṅgha of bhikkhus, there are bhikkhus with the three fetters wasted away, with greed, hatred and delusion reduced, once returners, who, having come to this world once, will make an end to suffering.

26
00:03:51,613 --> 00:03:52,973
[SPEAKER_00]: Such is this saṅgha of bhikkhus.

27
00:03:53,174 --> 00:03:57,176
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, in this saṅgha of bhikkhus, there are bhikkhus with the three fetters wasted away, stream-enterers,

28
00:03:58,210 --> 00:04:22,095
[SPEAKER_00]: of the nature of the lower realms certain of having an end in full awakening because there's such because in this saṅgha because so um so yes the uh the entire bhikkhu saṅgha there that the buddha um instructed beforehand that he said make the effort and reach the unreached attain the unattained realize the unrealized

29
00:04:22,987 --> 00:04:33,757
[SPEAKER_00]: There was an Arya Saṅgha, and it's important to note, well, we'll see why, but it's... there were no there were no putujanas in that assembly.

30
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:48,770
[SPEAKER_00]: So, for those who were not yet arahants, who still had work to do, then the Buddha decided, in this particular sutta, to to instruct on mindfulness of breathing.

31
00:04:50,591 --> 00:05:04,940
[SPEAKER_00]: Before he started, he listed all the ways that these bhikkhus, who are not shortened and sotāpannas, can do the rest of the work that they need to do and reach the unreached and so on.

32
00:05:05,841 --> 00:05:12,545
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, the bhikkhus... there are bhikkhus who dwell practicing the practice of the development of the four ways to set up mindfulness.

33
00:05:13,305 --> 00:05:15,087
[SPEAKER_00]: There are such bhikkhus in the Saṅgha of Bhikkhus.

34
00:05:15,287 --> 00:05:20,470
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the Noble... in the Noble Arya Saṅgha, there are bhikkhus who practice satipaṭṭhāna.

35
00:05:21,391 --> 00:05:37,702
[SPEAKER_00]: Then bhikkhus, in this saṅgha of bhikkhus, the noble saṅgha of bhikkhus, there are bhikkhus who dwell practicing the practice of development of the Four Right Efforts, the Four Foundations of Potency, the Five Strengths, the bhikkhus who practice Seven Factors of Awakening, the bhikkhus who practice the Noble Eightfold Path.

36
00:05:38,423 --> 00:05:40,564
[SPEAKER_00]: There are such bhikkhus in this saṅgha of bhikkhus.

37
00:05:42,385 --> 00:05:50,251
[SPEAKER_00]: In this saṅgha of bhikkhus, there are bhikkhus who dwell practicing the practice of development of loving-kindness, development of compassion, development of gladness,

38
00:05:51,008 --> 00:05:58,194
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all these relatively popular, or certainly familiar practices in contemporary Buddhism, are practiced by those who are not shorted in sotāpannas.

39
00:06:19,607 --> 00:06:26,589
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is something that Venerable Ñānavira was saying, but I said and I repeat it often.

40
00:06:27,109 --> 00:06:29,950
[SPEAKER_00]: You need the right view in order to know what to do.

41
00:06:30,550 --> 00:06:34,951
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, in order to know how to practice, you need to understand what the practice is.

42
00:06:35,631 --> 00:06:39,332
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just the most obvious reasoning.

43
00:06:39,592 --> 00:06:44,093
[SPEAKER_00]: You can arrive there by reasoning, that you can't do something unless you know what you're supposed to do.

44
00:06:45,729 --> 00:06:55,593
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why the Buddha insists on enlisting all these people who are there, then none of them, that's like pure heartwood, and none of them is shorter than like a sotāpanna.

45
00:06:56,233 --> 00:06:59,274
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, these are the practices that these noble disciples would do.

46
00:06:59,734 --> 00:07:03,496
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, that doesn't mean that the person shouldn't keep trying to understand what these practices are.

47
00:07:05,036 --> 00:07:08,438
[SPEAKER_00]: Because through understanding, you will become at least a sotāpanna.

48
00:07:09,298 --> 00:07:14,560
[SPEAKER_00]: But the problem is that in certainly in the contemporary Buddhism, the one that you hear a lot in the West,

49
00:07:15,585 --> 00:07:24,371
[SPEAKER_00]: People believe that automatically doing these things as some sort of technique or some sort of repetitive method, you will arrive at understanding.

50
00:07:25,711 --> 00:07:28,973
[SPEAKER_00]: But they can be done properly only by those who already understood it.

51
00:07:30,714 --> 00:07:36,138
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's sort of self-defeating, if it's done improperly.

52
00:07:36,198 --> 00:07:40,200
[SPEAKER_00]: So, eh...

53
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,381
[SPEAKER_00]: Which page are we on now?

54
00:07:48,443 --> 00:07:48,883
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, yeah.

55
00:07:49,283 --> 00:07:50,344
[SPEAKER_00]: So, let's get on.

56
00:07:50,364 --> 00:07:56,746
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it says, because in this saṅgha, because there are bhikkhus who dwell practicing practice of the development of mindfulness of breathing.

57
00:07:56,786 --> 00:08:00,928
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of breathing, when developed, made much of, is of great fruit, great benefit.

58
00:08:02,168 --> 00:08:06,530
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of breathing, when developed, made much of, fulfills the four ways to set up mindfulness.

59
00:08:06,550 --> 00:08:07,330
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's another thing.

60
00:08:07,510 --> 00:08:11,992
[SPEAKER_00]: Another contemporary, well-established perception.

61
00:08:12,514 --> 00:08:20,017
[SPEAKER_00]: When it comes to ānāpānasati, is that, eh... you do ānāpānasati in the form of watching your nostrils, or similar, and you enter the jhāna.

62
00:08:20,697 --> 00:08:26,579
[SPEAKER_00]: Automatically, you will eventually enter the jhāna, have the experience of jhāna through watching your nostrils.

63
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:36,363
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah... and here it is, THE sutta in question, the ānāpānasati sutta, and there's absolutely no mention of that whatsoever.

64
00:08:37,503 --> 00:08:42,085
[SPEAKER_00]: It says that by developing the mindfulness of breathing, you develop

65
00:08:42,763 --> 00:08:43,243
[SPEAKER_00]: Surprise!

66
00:08:43,683 --> 00:08:44,204
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness.

67
00:08:45,464 --> 00:08:47,705
[SPEAKER_00]: You develop the four foundations of mindfulness.

68
00:08:49,526 --> 00:08:53,708
[SPEAKER_00]: By developing the four foundations of mindfulness, you automatically get a jhāna.

69
00:08:54,088 --> 00:08:54,288
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

70
00:08:55,088 --> 00:08:57,669
[SPEAKER_00]: You develop the seven factors of awakening.

71
00:08:58,530 --> 00:09:02,911
[SPEAKER_00]: By developing seven factors of awakening, you develop wisdom and liberation.

72
00:09:03,132 --> 00:09:04,072
[SPEAKER_00]: You become an arahant.

73
00:09:05,678 --> 00:09:07,019
[SPEAKER_00]: In some other talks, that's...

74
00:09:07,139 --> 00:09:19,947
[SPEAKER_00]: I mentioned the relationship between ānāpānasati and jhāna, as in ānāpānasati, or many other ways of developing mindfulness, can serve as a basis for you to attend to the theme of jhāna, as the Buddha would describe.

75
00:09:20,008 --> 00:09:23,810
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, on account of that, develop mindfulness on the basis of breathing or something else.

76
00:09:24,250 --> 00:09:25,351
[SPEAKER_00]: Properly develop mindfulness.

77
00:09:25,913 --> 00:09:27,413
[SPEAKER_00]: You can develop theme of jhāna.

78
00:09:27,953 --> 00:09:36,135
[SPEAKER_00]: But thinking that doing a meditation method of watching your breath automatically results in jhāna, that all came much later, and it's certainly not found in the suttas.

79
00:09:37,695 --> 00:09:38,955
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, the Buddha carries on.

80
00:09:39,015 --> 00:09:39,856
[SPEAKER_00]: Developed in what way?

81
00:09:39,876 --> 00:09:41,496
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhu is made much of in what ways?

82
00:09:41,536 --> 00:09:44,116
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of breathing of much fruit, much benefit.

83
00:09:44,256 --> 00:09:52,538
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhu has gone to the forest, gone to the root of a tree, gone to an empty dwelling, sits down, having crossed leg... crossed his legs, making his back straight, having set up mindfulness in front.

84
00:09:54,044 --> 00:09:58,586
[SPEAKER_00]: We spoke about it in the first audio talk about mindfulness of the body.

85
00:09:59,606 --> 00:10:02,307
[SPEAKER_00]: So, just mindful he breathes in, just mindful he breathes out.

86
00:10:02,587 --> 00:10:04,768
[SPEAKER_00]: Breathing in long, he understands I'm breathing in long.

87
00:10:04,968 --> 00:10:07,549
[SPEAKER_00]: Breathing out long, he understands I'm breathing out long.

88
00:10:08,069 --> 00:10:10,250
[SPEAKER_00]: He's not focusing on what he's doing.

89
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:15,632
[SPEAKER_00]: He's not trying to attend and catch every moment and see things arising and passing away.

90
00:10:15,732 --> 00:10:17,553
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands what he's doing.

91
00:10:17,633 --> 00:10:19,193
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands what's occurring.

92
00:10:20,014 --> 00:10:21,014
[SPEAKER_00]: And in order for something...

93
00:10:21,722 --> 00:10:34,688
[SPEAKER_00]: In order for you to understand something, you cannot be absorbed in it, forcefully absorbed, even worse, prying upon like a... like a... like a... like a... like an owl trying to catch a fish.

94
00:10:36,109 --> 00:10:38,150
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to understand what's going on.

95
00:10:38,190 --> 00:10:44,793
[SPEAKER_00]: It means you already need to start paying attention to the nature of what's present, the nature of your action, in this case, the nature of breathing.

96
00:10:45,293 --> 00:10:46,894
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he understands what he's doing.

97
00:10:46,914 --> 00:10:49,855
[SPEAKER_00]: He's breathing in lung, he understands he's breathing in lung, and so on.

98
00:10:51,368 --> 00:10:54,711
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing the whole body, he trains.

99
00:10:54,751 --> 00:10:57,032
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe in as one who experiences the whole body.

100
00:10:57,353 --> 00:10:59,234
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, we mentioned that in the previous talk.

101
00:10:59,454 --> 00:11:07,300
[SPEAKER_00]: It's that body, that peripheral mindfulness, the image of the body that appears, that's discerned in that indirect manner within the...

102
00:11:08,121 --> 00:11:14,986
[SPEAKER_00]: I think I'll have to stop saying peripheral mindfulness, because it's just mindfulness, but... Well, I want to stop saying, but I can't, because obviously, if I say mindfulness,

103
00:11:16,688 --> 00:11:21,509
[SPEAKER_00]: People will regard that as coming under any idea of mindfulness that they might have.

104
00:11:23,009 --> 00:11:39,572
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the body, the imaginal body that appears in the peripheral mindfulness, the properly established mindfulness, eh... that's the body that you're trying to experience, without attending it, without making it a foreground, without making it an object.

105
00:11:41,232 --> 00:11:44,893
[SPEAKER_00]: And in the same manner, that's how you start calming the determinations of the body.

106
00:11:47,063 --> 00:11:49,684
[SPEAKER_00]: The determinations of that... those peripheral images.

107
00:11:50,745 --> 00:11:55,627
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same manner, I will breathe in as one who experiences joy, experiences pleasure.

108
00:11:57,288 --> 00:11:59,989
[SPEAKER_00]: It's all done on that background level.

109
00:12:00,649 --> 00:12:05,692
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, the more you discern the background, you realize how much input you can have in it.

110
00:12:06,952 --> 00:12:12,715
[SPEAKER_00]: Without overattending it, without trying to make it an object of your meditation, but discerning it for what it is.

111
00:12:18,183 --> 00:12:18,984
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, it carries on.

112
00:12:20,004 --> 00:12:22,986
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe in as one who experiences the determinations of the mind.

113
00:12:23,006 --> 00:12:28,130
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe out as one who experiences the determinations of the mind.

114
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:31,392
[SPEAKER_00]: Determinations of the mind being perception and feeling.

115
00:12:33,233 --> 00:12:37,837
[SPEAKER_00]: And you cannot possibly attend perception and feeling at the same time as a meditation object.

116
00:12:37,917 --> 00:12:41,439
[SPEAKER_00]: But you can certainly discern them in the periphery.

117
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:44,901
[SPEAKER_00]: Usually, it's the feeling that is discerned on the peripheral.

118
00:12:45,162 --> 00:12:46,162
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where the craving is.

119
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,183
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where everything else is.

120
00:12:48,858 --> 00:12:52,841
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I will breathe in as one who experiences that mind.

121
00:12:52,921 --> 00:12:56,244
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe out as the one who experiences that mind.

122
00:12:56,264 --> 00:12:57,385
[SPEAKER_00]: He will enjoy the mind.

123
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:59,226
[SPEAKER_00]: He will compose the mind.

124
00:12:59,326 --> 00:13:00,587
[SPEAKER_00]: He will liberate the mind.

125
00:13:01,128 --> 00:13:12,657
[SPEAKER_00]: The mind being the ultimate negative, the ultimate background, the ultimate general, the ultimate peripheral, determined by that which appears in front of your perception, by the feeling,

126
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:25,415
[SPEAKER_00]: That experience of those two things, that are simultaneously present in itself, that experience is the mind, and you cannot possibly attend to that, because that would require you to step outside of that mind, and then look at it as an object.

127
00:13:26,675 --> 00:13:35,177
[SPEAKER_00]: But you can certainly discern its outlines, and then discern its signs, the citta, nimitta, and that is all in that peripheral that we talk about very often.

128
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:43,138
[SPEAKER_00]: So, developed in this way, because made much of it in this way, mindfulness of breathing is of great fruit, great benefit.

129
00:13:45,377 --> 00:13:48,540
[SPEAKER_00]: And then it says, so, in what way bhikkhu is made mature?

130
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:53,004
[SPEAKER_00]: In what way does mindfulness of breathing fulfill the four ways to set up mindfulness?

131
00:13:54,485 --> 00:13:55,726
[SPEAKER_00]: The four satipaṭṭhānas.

132
00:13:56,747 --> 00:14:09,938
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, on whatever occasion, a bhikkhu breathing in long, understands and breathing in long, or breathing out long, understands and breathing out long, or breathing in short, understands and breathing in short, or breathing out short, understands and breathing out short.

133
00:14:11,944 --> 00:14:17,629
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu dwells as an observer of body in the body, ardent, aware, mindful, having removed covetousness and unhappiness in the world.

134
00:14:38,671 --> 00:14:42,194
[SPEAKER_00]: In this way, I speak of certain body within the bodies that is in and out breathing.

135
00:14:42,374 --> 00:14:50,439
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the body that you start discerning peripherally, on account of your mindfulness of in and out breathing, is that which stands for your experience of the body there.

136
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:55,963
[SPEAKER_00]: We said that before, but it certainly doesn't hurt repeating it.

137
00:14:56,143 --> 00:14:57,124
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, it goes further.

138
00:14:57,164 --> 00:15:04,830
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, on whatever occasion, bhikkhu trains, I will breathe in as the one who experiences joy, breathing as the one... breathing out as the one who experiences joy, and so on.

139
00:15:06,111 --> 00:15:08,012
[SPEAKER_00]: It says that then, on that occasion, the bhikkhu dwells

140
00:15:09,020 --> 00:15:11,082
[SPEAKER_00]: As an observer of feeling in feelings.

141
00:15:12,823 --> 00:15:19,188
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's a simultaneous presence of feeling within a feeling.

142
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:26,153
[SPEAKER_00]: Ardent, aware, mindful, having removed covetousness and unhappiness in the world.

143
00:15:26,574 --> 00:15:36,942
[SPEAKER_00]: And, by the way, when we talk about simultaneous presence, it doesn't mean there are two things simultaneously arisen for a second, or two, or a moment, and you must catch them.

144
00:15:37,697 --> 00:15:42,100
[SPEAKER_00]: Means that they endure on two different levels of generality.

145
00:15:42,861 --> 00:15:56,451
[SPEAKER_00]: Like a mood, for example, you can be in the same mood for two or three days, while on a more particular level, you can have various sort of fleeting perceptions or feelings of a lower kind.

146
00:15:56,591 --> 00:15:59,193
[SPEAKER_00]: And those two domains remain simultaneously present.

147
00:16:00,874 --> 00:16:06,018
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you become... if your mindfulness gets established upon the general mood,

148
00:16:11,601 --> 00:16:17,223
[SPEAKER_00]: You won't be affected and you will certainly be mindful automatically of all the things that arise within that.

149
00:16:17,903 --> 00:16:21,664
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's what it meant he's mindful of body within the body.

150
00:16:22,664 --> 00:16:26,546
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you're mindful or feeling within the feeling or feeling in the feeling.

151
00:16:27,166 --> 00:16:33,928
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when a person is mindful of the peripheral image of the body that they have, the body there out in the world,

152
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:42,494
[SPEAKER_00]: Any particular attention given to the body that appears as an object for you, that's within that body.

153
00:16:42,955 --> 00:16:49,659
[SPEAKER_00]: And you don't have to be chasing it or trying to not lose it, because that's automatically in the body that you are already mindful of.

154
00:16:49,779 --> 00:16:50,639
[SPEAKER_00]: Like a gatekeeper.

155
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:54,202
[SPEAKER_00]: You find a gate, and then you don't have to chase the things that go in.

156
00:16:54,662 --> 00:17:01,486
[SPEAKER_00]: You just stay at the gate, mindful, knowingly, that if you stay at the gate, you know exactly who is inside and who goes outside.

157
00:17:01,586 --> 00:17:02,887
[SPEAKER_00]: That was a simile from the suttas.

158
00:17:03,848 --> 00:17:05,529
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't mean you stare at the gate.

159
00:17:05,818 --> 00:17:06,499
[SPEAKER_00]: Like a robot.

160
00:17:06,819 --> 00:17:08,540
[SPEAKER_00]: Every second, try to not blink.

161
00:17:08,780 --> 00:17:10,262
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if you blink at the gate... No.

162
00:17:10,442 --> 00:17:12,804
[SPEAKER_00]: Just stand there, and you will know who passes.

163
00:17:12,984 --> 00:17:13,364
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

164
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:21,230
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's how a monk is properly mindful of feelings in the feelings, or feeling within the feeling.

165
00:17:23,052 --> 00:17:28,016
[SPEAKER_00]: You find the general feeling, which will then automatically include whatever is particularly felt.

166
00:17:28,636 --> 00:17:33,120
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not focusing hard on a particular feeling, and then try to discern feeling within that.

167
00:17:37,728 --> 00:17:44,254
[SPEAKER_00]: So bhikkhus, on whatever occasion bhikkhu trains, I will experience as the one who experiences the mind, I will breathe out as the one who experiences the mind.

168
00:17:44,654 --> 00:17:51,060
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu dwells as an observer of mind within the mind.

169
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:55,524
[SPEAKER_00]: Ardent, aware, mindful, having removed covetousness and unhappiness in the world.

170
00:17:56,204 --> 00:18:00,308
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, for the one who is forgetful, unaware, I do not speak of mindfulness of breathing.

171
00:18:02,545 --> 00:18:06,672
[SPEAKER_00]: On whatever occasion bhikkhu trains, I will breathe in as the one who sees impermanence.

172
00:18:06,872 --> 00:18:08,595
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe out as the one who sees impermanence.

173
00:18:08,795 --> 00:18:10,518
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe in as the one who sees dispassion.

174
00:18:10,858 --> 00:18:12,802
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe out as the one who sees dispassion.

175
00:18:13,022 --> 00:18:15,145
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe in as the one who sees cessation.

176
00:18:15,626 --> 00:18:17,409
[SPEAKER_00]: I will breathe out as the one who sees cessation.

177
00:18:18,040 --> 00:18:26,022
[SPEAKER_00]: That's basically when you discern the phenomenon of the peripheral, the dhamma of the peripheral, the nature of the peripheral, the nature of mindfulness, you automatically see that anything you attend within that experience is within that peripheral.

178
00:18:26,042 --> 00:18:29,423
[SPEAKER_00]: Those dhammas are already within these general dhammas.

179
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:56,226
[SPEAKER_00]: Having understood the general nature of a phenomenon, you have understood any single individual manifestation of that nature, i.e.

180
00:18:56,366 --> 00:18:57,787
[SPEAKER_00]: a particular phenomenon.

181
00:19:00,049 --> 00:19:05,954
[SPEAKER_00]: So, developed in this way, because made much in this way, mindfulness of breathing fulfills the four ways to set up mindfulness.

182
00:19:08,836 --> 00:19:16,722
[SPEAKER_00]: Then it says, eh... because in what way, made much of in what way, does the four ways of setting up mindfulness fulfill the seven factors of awakening?

183
00:19:17,848 --> 00:19:27,033
[SPEAKER_00]: Because on whatever occasion a bhikkhu dwells as an observer of body-in-body, ardent, aware, mindful, having removed covetousness and unhappiness in the world, on that occasion, having set up mindfulness, he is not forgetful.

184
00:19:27,774 --> 00:19:36,079
[SPEAKER_00]: Because on whatever occasion a bhikkhu's mindfulness is set up, he is not forgetful, on that occasion, a bhikkhu's mindfulness factor of awakening is aroused.

185
00:19:36,139 --> 00:19:38,980
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu develops the mindfulness factor of awakening.

186
00:19:40,241 --> 00:19:43,643
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu's mindfulness factor of awakening goes to fulfillment.

187
00:19:46,204 --> 00:19:47,265
[SPEAKER_00]: So, again,

188
00:19:47,821 --> 00:19:57,365
[SPEAKER_00]: If a person sort of has trouble understanding what we mean by mindfulness, peripheral mindfulness, dwell on the phenomenon of forgetfulness.

189
00:19:59,145 --> 00:20:12,570
[SPEAKER_00]: You remember things when you have a composure present in your mind, when it's like a general presence of your mind, not when you sort of are focusing on sight, sound, smell, taste, touches, sensations in your body.

190
00:20:12,991 --> 00:20:15,511
[SPEAKER_00]: That does not maintain your non-forgetfulness.

191
00:20:15,732 --> 00:20:16,952
[SPEAKER_00]: That actually takes you the way of

192
00:20:18,137 --> 00:20:26,763
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you don't want to find one point, like one-pointedness, often translated.

193
00:20:26,983 --> 00:20:42,073
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, you can call it one-pointedness, but there's a way of becoming one-pointed by focusing so hard on an object of your perception, even sensations, bodily sensations, which is just object of perception of touch, whereby you forget everything else.

194
00:20:42,673 --> 00:20:42,953
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

195
00:20:43,254 --> 00:20:45,255
[SPEAKER_00]: And sensuality works exactly the same way.

196
00:20:45,645 --> 00:20:51,168
[SPEAKER_00]: When the mind gets bent on having something, you pretty much lose perspective on everything else.

197
00:20:51,869 --> 00:21:04,276
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, there is the one-pointedness that we talk about, which is you find a more general point, like the domain of the peripheral, for example, the background of your experience, that then automatically includes everything else.

198
00:21:06,197 --> 00:21:09,959
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not the one-pointedness that makes you absorbed, so you forget everything else.

199
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:12,741
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the one-pointedness that there's nothing left out.

200
00:21:13,361 --> 00:21:14,342
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything is included.

201
00:21:19,168 --> 00:21:20,869
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, then he goes further.

202
00:21:22,650 --> 00:21:23,891
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how to develop mindfulness.

203
00:21:23,911 --> 00:21:31,075
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, dwelling mindful in this way, he thinks about, he ponders over, he undergoes an investigation of a phenomena.

204
00:21:33,016 --> 00:21:35,598
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, that is pretty self-explanatory.

205
00:21:35,918 --> 00:21:39,160
[SPEAKER_00]: You actually actively make the effort to think and understand.

206
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:42,882
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the only way the understanding can come about, and with mindfulness.

207
00:21:44,025 --> 00:21:49,426
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he may... he undergoes an investigation of that phenomenon with an understanding.

208
00:21:49,486 --> 00:21:56,288
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, on whatever occasion, bhikkhu dwelling mindful in this way, thinks about, ponders over, undergoes an investigation of the phenomena with an understanding.

209
00:21:56,328 --> 00:22:01,269
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu... bhikkhu's investigation of phenomena, factor of awakening, is aroused.

210
00:22:01,349 --> 00:22:02,069
[SPEAKER_00]: Dhamma vijaya.

211
00:22:03,189 --> 00:22:07,430
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu develops the investigation of phenomena, factor of awakening.

212
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:18,187
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, for one, thinking about, pondering over, undergoing an investigation of the phenomena, understanding, active energy is aroused.

213
00:22:19,328 --> 00:22:26,515
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu's thinking about, pondering over, undergoing an investigation of that phenomena, with an understanding, active energy is aroused.

214
00:22:26,535 --> 00:22:31,680
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu's energy factor of awakening is aroused.

215
00:22:31,700 --> 00:22:34,944
[SPEAKER_00]: That energy factor of awakening goes to fulfillment.

216
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:41,622
[SPEAKER_00]: For the one with energy aroused, a joy not of the flesh arises.

217
00:22:42,602 --> 00:22:45,643
[SPEAKER_00]: Means a joy not of a bodily kind.

218
00:22:47,904 --> 00:22:50,185
[SPEAKER_00]: And what joy is not of a bodily kind?

219
00:22:51,325 --> 00:22:54,147
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the joy of knowledge, joy of discernment, joy of peace.

220
00:22:56,327 --> 00:22:58,868
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's in the background of that which is your body.

221
00:22:59,809 --> 00:23:01,509
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there is no other body where it could be.

222
00:23:01,969 --> 00:23:03,390
[SPEAKER_00]: No other space for it to be.

223
00:23:03,610 --> 00:23:06,091
[SPEAKER_00]: So it's either in the body or it's in your mindfulness of the body.

224
00:23:08,492 --> 00:23:17,238
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, on whatever occasion that joy arises, the body calms down, and then the mind calms down.

225
00:23:17,738 --> 00:23:21,901
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu's tranquility factor of awakening is aroused.

226
00:23:23,441 --> 00:23:26,603
[SPEAKER_00]: With a tranquil body, for one who is happy, the mind is composed.

227
00:23:27,864 --> 00:23:33,788
[SPEAKER_00]: On whatever occasion, for a bhikkhu with a tranquil body, for one who is happy, the mind is composed.

228
00:23:33,868 --> 00:23:36,990
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu's composure factor of awakening is aroused.

229
00:23:38,162 --> 00:23:43,346
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu develops the composure factor of awakening, and that composure factor goes to fulfillment.

230
00:23:44,887 --> 00:23:49,711
[SPEAKER_00]: He is the one who looks on properly at the mind composed in this way.

231
00:23:49,751 --> 00:23:53,675
[SPEAKER_00]: On whatever occasion, a bhikkhu is the one who looks on properly at the mind composed in this way.

232
00:23:53,715 --> 00:23:57,918
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu's indifference factor of awakening is aroused.

233
00:23:57,978 --> 00:23:58,478
[SPEAKER_00]: Upeka.

234
00:23:59,099 --> 00:24:02,922
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the bhikkhu develops the indifference factor of awakening.

235
00:24:02,962 --> 00:24:05,164
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the indifference factor goes to fulfillment.

236
00:24:07,001 --> 00:24:20,526
[SPEAKER_00]: bhikkhus, on whatever occasion, bhikkhu dwells as an observer of feeling and feeling, mind and mind, phenomena and phenomena, ardent, aware, mindful, having removed covetousness and unhappiness in the world, in regard to the world, on that occasion, having set up mindfulness, he is not forgetful.

237
00:24:25,288 --> 00:24:29,369
[SPEAKER_00]: And he goes to repeat dhamma, vijaya, and so on.

238
00:24:32,771 --> 00:24:35,892
[SPEAKER_00]: And he said, in what way, because

239
00:24:36,434 --> 00:24:41,476
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, the seven factors of enlightenment... of awakening fulfill wisdom and liberation.

240
00:24:41,556 --> 00:24:49,180
[SPEAKER_00]: Here, Bhikkhu Zubikkhu develops the mindfulness factor of awakening, supported by seclusion, supported by dispassion, supported by cessation, resulting in relinquishment.

241
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:59,724
[SPEAKER_00]: He develops the investigational phenomena factor of the awakening, the energy factor of awakening, the joy factor of awakening, develops the tranquility factor of awakening, develops the composure factor of awakening.

242
00:25:00,024 --> 00:25:06,287
[SPEAKER_00]: He develops the indifference factor of awakening, supported by seclusion, supported by dispassion, supported by cessation, resulting in relinquishment.

243
00:25:07,309 --> 00:25:13,391
[SPEAKER_00]: Developed in this way, the same factors awakening fulfill the wisdom and liberation, full understanding.

244
00:25:13,491 --> 00:25:14,492
[SPEAKER_00]: One becomes an Arahant.

245
00:25:16,552 --> 00:25:19,373
[SPEAKER_00]: So that concludes this Ānāpānasati Sutta.

246
00:25:21,314 --> 00:25:33,698
[SPEAKER_00]: And, yeah, this audio can go in conjunction with the mindfulness of the body, certainly the part one of that, of those audio notes, because it's... lots of things that I mentioned, they are fully applicable here.

247
00:25:36,549 --> 00:25:53,837
[SPEAKER_00]: Most notably, obviously, that one needs to have the right view in order to do this practice correctly, and to stop expecting an automatic result of some sort of experience, confused to be jhāna, coming out of watching the nostrils, or watching the belly, or whichever way people do mindfulness of breathing today.

248
00:25:54,598 --> 00:25:59,880
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of breathing is about understanding the nature of action of breathing.

249
00:25:59,900 --> 00:26:00,741
[SPEAKER_00]: You could say it like that.

250
00:26:01,341 --> 00:26:05,083
[SPEAKER_00]: It's understanding, like, I'm breathing in long, I understand I'm breathing in long.

251
00:26:05,562 --> 00:26:07,864
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't have to keep telling to myself that I'm breathing in lung.

252
00:26:08,284 --> 00:26:11,647
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't have to keep attending every, every second of that breath.

253
00:26:11,727 --> 00:26:11,987
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

254
00:26:12,047 --> 00:26:14,929
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of that, of that breath.

255
00:26:15,430 --> 00:26:19,713
[SPEAKER_00]: Because I understand what I'm doing, while I'm doing it.

256
00:26:20,133 --> 00:26:21,635
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the essence of mindfulness.

257
00:26:22,375 --> 00:26:28,600
[SPEAKER_00]: Knowing what you're doing, while you're doing it, means being peripherally aware of what's directly happening.

258
00:26:30,982 --> 00:26:32,323
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that should be enough for now.

